\f1\fs32\b GrowthForge AI \endash Google Ads Integration Design\b0\f0\fs24\par
\par
\b Company:\b0 Strapli Technologies Inc.\par
\b Product:\b0 GrowthForge AI (usegrowthforge.com)\par
\b API Usage:\b0 Google Ads API (Read + Campaign Management)\par
\par

\f1\fs28\b 1. Tool Overview\b0\f0\fs24\par
\par
GrowthForge AI is a marketing automation SaaS platform that serves as a complete AI marketing department for small and medium-sized businesses. Users connect their Google Ads accounts to the platform via OAuth 2.0 to import real campaign performance data.\par
\par

\f1\fs28\b 2. Google Ads API Feature: Campaign Manager\b0\f0\fs24\par
\par
\b Feature Name:\b0 Campaign Manager \endash Google Ads Sync\par
\b Location:\b0 Project Dashboard > Campaign Manager tab\par
\par
\b User Flow:\b0\par
1. User navigates to Campaign Manager inside their GrowthForge project\par
2. A \ldblquote Connect Google Ads\rdblquote  banner is displayed at the top of the page\par
3. User clicks \ldblquote Connect Google Ads\rdblquote  \endash initiates OAuth 2.0 consent flow\par
4. User grants permission on Google\rquote s OAuth consent screen (scope: adwords)\par
5. Platform stores refresh token securely; user is redirected back to Campaign Manager\par
6. User sees their connected account info (email, customer ID, last sync time)\par
7. User clicks \ldblquote Sync Now\rdblquote  to pull latest campaign data\par
8. Platform fetches campaign metrics via Google Ads API GAQL query (last 30 days)\par
9. Campaigns appear in the dashboard with real metrics: impressions, clicks, conversions, spend, CTR, CPC, ROAS\par
\par

\f1\fs28\b 3. Data Accessed from Google Ads API\b0\f0\fs24\par
\par
\b Read-only data fetched:\b0\par
\bullet  Campaign name, ID, status, channel type\par
\bullet  Metrics (last 30 days): impressions, clicks, conversions, cost_micros, CTR, average CPC\par
\par
\b GAQL Query Used:\b0\par
\i SELECT campaign.id, campaign.name, campaign.status, campaign.advertising_channel_type, metrics.impressions, metrics.clicks, metrics.conversions, metrics.cost_micros, metrics.ctr, metrics.average_cpc FROM campaign WHERE segments.date DURING LAST_30_DAYS AND campaign.status != 'REMOVED' ORDER BY metrics.impressions DESC LIMIT 50\i0\par
\par

\f1\fs28\b 4. OAuth Scope\b0\f0\fs24\par
\par
Scope requested: \b https://www.googleapis.com/auth/adwords\b0\par
Auth type: OAuth 2.0 with offline access (refresh token stored server-side)\par
Redirect URI: https://usegrowthforge.com/api/auth/google-ads/callback\par
\par

\f1\fs28\b 5. Data Storage & Security\b0\f0\fs24\par
\par
\bullet  OAuth tokens stored server-side in PostgreSQL database (never exposed to client)\par
\bullet  Access tokens refreshed automatically on expiry using stored refresh token\par
\bullet  Campaign data cached in platform database; synced on user request\par
\bullet  Users can disconnect their Google Ads account at any time (tokens immediately deleted)\par
\par

\f1\fs28\b 6. Target Users\b0\f0\fs24\par
\par
\bullet  Small and medium-sized businesses running Google Ads campaigns\par
\bullet  Marketing agencies managing Google Ads for multiple clients\par
\bullet  Users access the tool through their GrowthForge account (authentication required)\par
\par
\b Access model:\b0 Each GrowthForge user connects their own Google Ads account. The platform never accesses accounts without explicit OAuth authorization from the account owner.\par
\par
